.TH Command NEWS
.SY "news <DAYS>"
The news command prints a copy of the local newspaper published by
The Empire News.
.s3
This "morning after" daily recounts financial exploits,
the telegram traffic between countries,
and political maneuvering
in addition to the chronicling of such mundanities as shelling, attacking,
and nuclear testing.
.s3
It's great breakfast reading!
.s3
Normally your edition of the news will only contain events that have
occurred since you last read the news.
You can specify what time period you'd like it to cover with the optional
"<DAYS>" argument in the command line as in:
.s3
.EX news 2
Which will print the news for the last two days.
.s3
See also : headlines
